!! "No Global Now" — the operator's own sentences, dated

''The attribution the house carries.'' The boot seed seats the law under #/causal-islands and names its source: //"''No global now'' (Fuller). The Universe holds no global now; each island carries its own partially-ordered log and knows only //as of my last sync//, never //globally//."// The operator names the same lineage in the FFZ chronometer's own expansion — //"FFZ chronometer (Fontany Fuller Zelenka clock, no global now)"// (2026-06-25).

''Every operator instance the mines surfaced, in order, quote license:''

# ''2026-06-25'' — //"talk story through our model and if the FFZ chronometer (Fontany Fuller Zelenka cloickk with no global now) fits into this kupono model at high mana/manao?"// — ASKS. Seats the clock's name around the law rather than beside it.
# ''2026-06-29'' — //"Now we need a research swarm to figure out the missing scale defiitions in our FFZ clock as applied to mempalace stores. 'No global now' holds, L-Prime holds."// — RULES the law as a standing constraint on a design pass, paired with the ward.
# ''2026-06-30'' — //"I reject the capturedTime (Date.now()) as an anchor for the fFZ, that reads un-pono to 'no global now causal islands'. Think through this … send a research spirit to find the most pono 'no global now' rhymthmic schema. Real questions are the very top level ~ what can we pin it to that's not 'the human ratchetts that scale'?"// — ''RULES, and it rules a REJECTION'': a wall-clock reading MUST NOT anchor a grain. The cure landed as nested-membership with no wall time (`8e6d4fdd`).
# ''2026-07-01'' — //"ensure we align with the web3 laws of the repo, \"no global now\", \"causal islands\", \"nested nameless entities with #has caps\", and our other Pono intent vectors"// — RULES the law as a standing audit axis.
# ''2026-07-06'' — ''THE FORK-4 SENTENCE'' — //"4. I really want to avoid ANY hard attachments to wall-clocks (soft \"unrealiable-witness-timestamp\" seems pono). This may need a internet research deep knowledge domain \"find the pattern integrities that ryme with the missing puzzle piece\" to resolve."// — ''RULES the direction and commissions the research'' that produced #/the-ruling. Read the two halves apart: //ANY hard attachment// refused; a //soft// unreliable-witness timestamp allowed.
# ''2026-07-17'' — //"Pono, 'no global now', 'causal islands', and 'pet-name tagged nameless-entities with #has capability stacks' serves as our core pattern integrity triangle."// — ''RULES the law's RANK'': one of three legs, not a preference.
# ''2026-07-17'' (the HINGE) — //"We can have 'shared public Cabal/org documents posted to the @crossroads layer of the dreamNet' but they MUST retain our base web3 causal island 'no global now' intent (unable to scrape 'person history/registry' etc), but a publicly availalble 'surface'."// — RULES that a PUBLIC surface inherits the law; it names the law's second face, //no aggregable registry//.
# ''2026-08-08'' — //"Approved, but no 'rosters' remember? Only contracts (no global now, causal island shores, web3-but-not-finance-illth).)"// — ''RULES: a roster carries a global now.'' Carried forward verbatim as a standing constraint in every later session summary.
# ''2026-08-12'' — //"We lean toward requiring a raise on every boot. \"No global now/protection against empire/web3-but-not-illth-crypto\" lead the way here."// — LEANS, and names the law as a tie-breaker between designs.
# ''2026-08-13'' — //"Aah pono, language itself has no global now (authority), we each carry our own maps at our personal resolution/grains/capabilities."// — the operator's own GLOSS: ''global now ≡ authority''. The sharpest one-line reading of the law the mines hold.
# ''2026-08-16'' — //"no global now/causal island law MUST hold. scout again all domains (repo/internet), then plan & enact if you hold high confidence"// — RULES, RFC-2119 grade.
# ''2026-08-16'' (a correction) — //"Does this read 'no global now' (wallclock on each device serves as an unreliable narrator)?"// — ASKS, and the asking carried the cure; see #/expiry.
# ''2026-08-30'' — ''THE THREAT MODEL'' — //"Sounds good but we must resolve the \"not gl8bal now\" tension (wall clock timestamps simply cannot get relied on, red-team testers can set them arbitrarily). OODA-HA"// — ''RULES the REASON'': the wall clock reads as an ATTACKER-CONTROLLED input, not merely an imprecise one.
# ''2026-08-31'' — //"humans never get \"pinned\" to a data entity in our no global now causal island schema & all \"identity gets enacted as relation\""// — RULES the law's reach into identity.
# ''2026-09-08'' — on differential testing: //"\"The results of two tested programs may differ and yet still be correct.\" -> No Global Now."// — the operator READS the law outside distributed systems entirely; agreement names a sync, never a truth.
# ''2026-09-13'' — //"\"No Global Now\" holds."// — the charge this carrier answers. RULES that nothing in the two gaps reopens the law.

''The settled sense, as the operator has spoken it'' — three claims, each resting on a sentence above, never on the scout's reading:

* ''No authority of time.'' A global now names an AUTHORITY (2026-08-13). The law forbids the authority, not the reading of a clock.
* ''A wall clock reads as a hostile narrator.'' Not slow, not skewed — ''settable by an adversary'' (2026-08-30). So no SAFETY verdict may rest on one.
* ''A roster carries a global now'' (2026-08-08). Any construct that needs "who existed, at an agreed moment" re-imports the law's violation by another door.

