<<~ ahu #/the-ruling>>

!! The ruling — Fork-4, resolved 2026-07-06

''Provenance.'' The operator's Fork-4 sentence (2026-07-06, #/no-global-now §5) commissioned two research spirits — CHRONO-WISP (logical time and fencing) and WITNESS-WISP (witnessed and soft time). Both converged; the house folded them the same evening, and the resolution stands recorded in `project_clockless_lease_model.md`. The mines hold no later operator sentence that reopens it.

''The ruling's own words'' (quote license, `project_clockless_lease_model.md`, 2026-07-06):

> ''SAFETY = pure logical, clock-free, always-on.'' corm is a FENCING TOKEN, not a timer … A grant carries `(corm-epoch, ITC-stamp, ⟨soft: FfzClock-grain⟩)`. The GUARDED RESOURCE … holds `highest-corm-admitted` and REJECTS any invocation whose epoch < high-water OR whose ITC-stamp is causally dominated by an already-admitted one. A paused/forwarded/replayed holder self-revokes the instant a higher epoch touches the resource — NO global broadcast, NO clock. ''Expiry = SUPERSESSION ("a higher epoch exists downstream of me"), NEVER "a duration elapsed."''

> ''LIVENESS = soft, local, adaptive.'' … it reduces to a LOCAL, monotone, roughly-uniform oscillator feeding ''φ-accrual failure detection'' … Quarantine: (a) the tick lives INSIDE one causal island; (b) feeds ONLY suspicion/liveness, NEVER safety/ordering; (c) never leaves the island as a timestamp others must agree on.

> ''WITNESS = the gossip surface, Roughtime-shaped'' … each witness returns a SIGNED (epoch, radius) … the puller sends a FRESH NONCE … "a stamp with no fresh challenge is a photograph of a clock" … The witness supplies rough cross-checked RATE calibration … ONLY when a soft physical rate is needed — radius-tagged, never authoritative.

> ''/oracle pointer = IPNS-MINUS-RFC3339.'' Keep `Sequence` (≡ corm-epoch …). Selection = highest-epoch-wins (ITC breaks concurrency ties). REPLACE the RFC3339 EOL Validity with a SUPERSESSION rule ("live until a higher-Sequence record appears") + an OPTIONAL soft FfzClock-grain hint … that reads as ADVICE, never a hard gate.

> ''ONE-LINE INVARIANT:'' safety rides ITC + corm (causal, monotone, clock-free); liveness rides FfzClock-as-φ (rhythmic suspicion, local, soft); the two NEVER cross wires. "Order is free; rate costs a seed."

''The five warnings, the ruling's own numbering'' (quote license):

# ''MANDATE resource-side fencing (high-water-mark) or the whole model is nothing — a resource that doesn't fence lets two holders act.''
# SPLIT-BRAIN … ''ITC MUST adjudicate concurrency'' + a deterministic tiebreak … ''Ask ITC for concurrency, NEVER FfzClock.''
# ''Lint that the soft witness field never colors an ordering/revocation branch — the moment code branches on it for those, the global-now is back.''
# ''rough⊥tight'' … never ask the rough layer for a tight guarantee — a lease must be epoch-generous vs the witness radius.
# ''Bootstrap:'' a cold node with no witnesses/anchor accepts first sync as Provisional (never Canon).

''Three amendments the house landed AFTER the ruling, each dated:''

* ''φ-accrual's wall-time, named and confined (2026-08-15).'' A research pass collided the ledger: //"φ-accrual carries wall-time inside it. That ledger entry and the 'no wall-clock durations' law cannot both stand."// A measuring pass the same day found the collision ''moot in code'' — `grep -rin "accrual\|phiAccrual"` over `packages/**/*.ts` returned ''zero hits''; `clock-recovery.ts:1-3` stands the opposite discipline in its own comment (//"recovers the FFZ rhythmic clock FROM the fed stream (no Date.now, no global now)… never a wall-clock timestamp"//). ''Nothing needs unwinding; something needs never-building.'' Roughtime likewise stands ''cited and unbuilt'' — the same pass found zero implementation, zero dependency, zero test.
* ''THE ACCRUAL IMPOSSIBILITY (2026-08-15, and it does not yield).'' <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/lamplighters">> states it: //"''a logical epoch cannot accrue silence at all'' — a per-writer max-register advances only when somebody writes, so ''the neglected herm's counter stops at exactly the moment neglect begins''. Any clockless accrual MUST ride a monotone quantity driven by parties other than the neglected one."//
* ''THE FOURTH OPTION, and the clockless-verdict fork RULED (operator, 2026-09-11).'' <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/field-collision">> `:117` records it: //"THE CLOCKLESS-VERDICT FORK — RULED (operator, 2026-09-11): READ FREE, ACT BY CONTRACT … the ahi kā reading stays a log-fact plus attenuation ALWAYS: clockless, accusing nobody."// The mechanism that escapes the impossibility reads as a ''RATIO against an INDEPENDENT ambient'' — the realm still while a motion it cannot drive advanced by K — never a duration (`ahi-ka.ts` header). The numeric half stands RATIFIED the same way (operator, 2026-09-13): `ambientFloor 8 · warmRatio 0.30 · coldRatio 0.05`, //"fiction-QA defaults"//.

''So the liveness leg the ruling named φ-accrual has MOVED, by ruling, to a ratio-against-an-ambient; the safety leg and the witness leg stand as written.''

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/supersession>>

!! Supersession — what the house means by the word

''The candidates the charge names, answered from the mines:''

| reading | does the house name it the validity gate? | where |
|---|---|---|
| a newer lease under the same corm (a higher epoch appears) | ''YES — this one'' | the ruling; `waking-floor:163`, `:203-205`; `device-delegation.ts:183-185` |
| an ITC dominance | NO — ITC adjudicates ''CONCURRENCY and the tiebreak'', never the gate | ruling warning (2) |
| a φ-accrual verdict | NO — it feeds ''suspicion only'', and crossing that wire IS the failure | ruling, LIVENESS quarantine (b) |
| a hand's explicit act | NO — that names ''targeted revocation'', a different mechanism | `epoch-lease.ts:6-8`; `convergent-mesh#two-revocation-modes` |

''The ruling's own gate sentence'': //"Expiry = SUPERSESSION ('a higher epoch exists downstream of me'), NEVER 'a duration elapsed.'"// And for the pointer specifically: //"live until a higher-Sequence record appears"//.

''The house has already written this law once, for the sibling grant type.'' <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/waking-floor">> `:163` (quote license): //"''AND THE RAISE ENDS BY SUPERSESSION, never by a duration.'' A first cut expressed the expiry as a wall-clock interval, which fails twice: two islands with different clocks disagree about whether a raise stands, and a vessel AT THE FLOOR holds no trustworthy wall time at all … A paused, forwarded or replayed raise ''self-revokes the instant a higher epoch lands'' — no broadcast, no clock … ''Fusing the two wires is how a global now gets smuggled back in.''"//

''And it names the MECHANISM, refusing a third invention'' (`waking-floor:201-205`): //"A raise ENDS by non-renewal, exactly as every other grant in this house does. `raiseStands` reads `boundEpoch >= effective` against the Nexus's own lease epoch — the same comparison, against the same fold, that `device-delegation` already makes. The Nexus is the resource; its lease epoch is the fence. Supersession and expiry come from that one mechanism, with no clock anywhere."//

''One shape STRUCK, and the striking matters'' (`waking-floor:207`): a draft carried a ''rolling WINDOW of markers'' as the epoch. //"A set answers //is this listed// and never //is this newer//, so a partitioned island could not reason about it locally; whatever fell off its far end encoded a retention policy nobody wrote; and a list of valid markers is a roster of moments, which this house does not hold."// ''A supersession cure MUST NOT reach for a set.'' It reads a scalar max-register (`epoch-lease.ts`: `effectiveLeaseEpoch` = max over per-writer slots, //"the max never decreases"//).

''What supersession therefore asks of the oracle pointer, in the house's own terms'': the reader compares the pointer's `version` (≡ the corm epoch, ≡ `Sequence`) against the highest version it holds for that object, and refuses ONLY what sits below. A pointer nothing has out-versioned stands live however long a clock has moved.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/expiry>>

!! Does `expiry` survive — and in what shape

''The mines answer YES, and the house already spells it three different ways, each lawful, each NAMED.''

!!! ① The BACKSTOP spelling — `device-delegation.ts`, and the operator's own question produced it

The operator asked (2026-08-16, quote license): //"Does this read 'no global now' (wallclock on each device serves as an unreliable narrator)?"// The house's answer and cure that turn: ''the lease is the authority, the clock only backstops'' — and the code now says it in its own comments (quote license):

* `device-delegation.ts:66` — `expiresAt` — //"ISO-8601 expiry instant — bounds the replay window even absent synchronous revocation (now a replay ''BACKSTOP'', not the lease authority)."//
* `device-delegation.ts:177-180` — //"The epoch is the lease ''AUTHORITY''; the wall-clock window above is only a replay backstop. Targeted revocation rides the Keyhive membership graph, never this counter."//
* And the RANKING rides the call site: `verifyDeviceDelegation(edge, root, { now, expectedEpoch })` — the comment at the time of the cure read //"`now` — replay backstop — the unreliable narrator"// beside //"`expectedEpoch` — THE AUTHORITY — monotone, local, no shared clock"//, with two tests fencing the ranking (a grant bound below a rolled lease refuses ''while the wall clock still reads inside its window'').

''The sin that cure named, in the house's own words'': //"The violation is that I made the unreliable narrator the ONLY narrator."// That sentence prices gap (2) exactly.

!!! ② The ROLLS spelling — an `expiry` read against the realm's own pace

* `realm-bag.ts:114-120` — //"The registration's LEASE, in ROLLS of the realm's own maintenance feed (`realmPace` — an order, never a wall-clock instant). Past it the WRITE side lapses and the book reads on."// The reader that names no pace //"reads the lease as unexpired (it cannot judge, so it never narrows)"// (`:137-142`) — ''fail-open toward standing, exactly as `readAhiKa` abstains''.
* `cas-caps.ts:1-6` — the PIN and PREFETCH caps: //"Both name a holder and an expiry; both read the expiry against the realm's own clock (`graceForTier` in rolls of `realmPace`), never a wall-clock alone."//

!!! ③ The NAMED-FLOOR spelling — when a wall clock rides, the code says so

`bag-residency.ts:126-132`, `:182`, `:195` — `BagStowage` takes an optional realm `clock` (rolls, `DEFAULT_IDLE_ROLLS = 8`, matching ahi kā's `ambientFloor`); absent one it //"falls to the wall floor and names it"// as `clockKind: "realm" | "wall-floor"`. <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/handoff">> `:533` records the close (2026-09-12): the fallback gets named //"rather than claiming a clocklessness it does not hold. The browser vessel wires no realm clock and stays on the named floor — ''a declared partial, not a silent one''."//

!!! What the ORACLE POINTER carries today, against those three

`oracle-substrate.ts:50` — `expiry: number` — //"ms epoch; freshness lease read against the LOCAL clock"//; minted at `oracle-read-face.ts:91` and `bulb-read-face.ts:146` as `Date.now() + TTL_MS`; gated at `oracle-substrate.ts:~196` by `if (opts.nowMs >= p.expiry) return { ok: false, reason: "expired" }`. It signs the expiry into the pointer (//"a peer must not be able to extend a stale pointer's life"//) while holding it OUT of the pointer's identity string, so a renewal keeps the lineage — a genuinely careful design that nonetheless seats the unreliable narrator as the ''only'' narrator on that branch.

''The reconciliation the mines support'' (and no further): the pointer's `expiry` joins spelling ① — a REPORTED replay backstop that MAY refuse, never the validity authority — or spelling ② if a pace reader reaches it. ''The mines hold no sentence letting it stay the gate.''

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-fence>>

!! Is the FENCE mandatory in the ruling's own words

''Yes, in the ruling's text — and in the strongest register it uses anywhere.'' Warning (1), verbatim: //"''MANDATE resource-side fencing (high-water-mark) or the whole model is nothing'' — a resource that doesn't fence lets two holders act."// The ruling's SAFETY paragraph repeats it as mechanism, not advice: the guarded resource //"holds `highest-corm-admitted` and REJECTS any invocation whose epoch < high-water"//.

''And the ruling left the fence's REACH as its own named design-time question'' (quote license, the OPEN block): //"does EVERY /oracle read-face + capability endpoint already hold (or cheaply can hold) a per-object high-water mark? ''(any that can't = where a clock sneaks back)''"// — the probe `e2da729e4` answered it, which is exactly why the probe exists.

''What the code does with `highWaterVersion` today.'' `oracle-substrate.ts:~155` — //"`highWaterVersion`: the highest version this reader has accepted; a lower one reads as a ROLLBACK and gets refused"// — ''OPTIONAL'' (`highWaterVersion?: number`). `oracle-read-client.ts:82-88` forwards it only when the caller supplies it, and `nowMs` defaults to `Date.now()` (`:68`). So a reader may verify with ''no fence at all'' and cannot ask for a ''clock-free verdict'' — the inversion the probe pinned.

''Two things the mines separate, and the carrier keeps apart.'' The ruling MANDATES that the guarded RESOURCE fence. Whether the pure `verifyOraclePointer` FUNCTION must refuse a caller who names no high-water names a different question — an API shape, not a law — and the mines carry no sentence on it. See #/silence and #/questions.

''The precedent one layer over, for whoever builds it.'' `device-delegation.ts` also leaves `expectedEpoch` optional (//"OPTIONAL (like opts.now): pass expectedEpoch … to enforce the lease; omit to check signature + pin alone"//) and cures the inversion at the ''call site'', by ranking the two instruments in the caller's own code. The oracle pointer's asymmetry differs from that precedent in one measurable way: `nowMs` there reads optional too, while on the pointer it stands ''required''.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/silence>>

!! Where the operator's intent runs SILENT

''This carrier fills none of these.''

# ''The API shape of the fence.'' The operator has never spoken on whether a pure verify FUNCTION must REFUSE a fence-less caller, or whether a required-`highWater` / optional-`nowMs` swap suffices. Warning (1) belongs to the spirits' fold, blessed by the operator's approval of the whole resolution, and it binds ''the resource'', not a signature.
# ''Whether the oracle pointer's `expiry` keeps a wall-ms floor at all, or moves to rolls.'' The three spellings at #/expiry all stand lawful in the house. Nothing in the mines picks among them for THIS object.
# ''Who mints corm epochs per resource.'' The ruling records it OPEN in its own words — //"single-owner (Raft-leader) vs any-forwarder (needs ITC concurrency + tiebreak, making ITC-concurrency load-bearing not optional)"//. No later sentence settles it. The oracle pointer today reads single-signer by construction (`signerSeed`), which ANSWERS the question by omission rather than by ruling.
# ''Whether ITC rides the oracle pointer at all.'' The ruling's selection rule names //"highest-epoch-wins (ITC breaks concurrency ties)"//; `oracle-substrate.ts` carries no ITC stamp, and a same-version fork today surfaces only through the `prev` lineage check. The mines hold no sentence saying that suffices.
# ''Roughtime.'' Named WITNESS in the ruling, measured ''zero-implementation'' 2026-08-15, and flagged 2026-09-11 as wanting //"lists of trusted servers, i.e. a roster"// — which #/no-global-now §8 forbids. The mines hold the tension NAMED and unruled.
# ''The soft FfzClock-grain hint.'' The ruling allows //"an OPTIONAL soft FfzClock-grain hint that reads as ADVICE, never a hard gate"//. Nothing in the mines asks for it to be built, and nothing forbids it.

