<<~ ahu #/pattern-integrity-rhymes>>

!! Pattern-integrity rhymes the house already carries

Each row names what the house built, how it rhymes with the lease, and where it BREAKS against it.

| the rhyme | what it does | rhymes with the lease | breaks against it |
|---|---|---|---|
| ''the stowage clock'' (`bag-residency.ts:126-195`) | cools a bag after `idle` in the realm's ROLLS when a clock rides in; else the wall floor, ''named'' `clockKind: "wall-floor"` | the same two-tier shape the lease wants: logical unit first, wall as a declared fallback; and it cites the lamplighters ban in its own comment | nowhere. It even keeps the RESIDENCY sense (a vessel's own RAM pressure, a legitimate local wall reading) apart from a STANDING verdict — the cross-plane leak `handoff:533` closed |
| ''the CAS sweep'' (`node-cas.ts:222-338`, `cas-caps.ts`) | sweeps at a cadence paced by the realm's roll rate, ''abstaining under two rolls'' — //"a realm nobody feeds never sweeps — never a calendar"// | supersession's own temper: no motion, no ageing. Grace counts ROLLS, so //"a day of silence ages nothing"// | one honest seam its own hand named: the pace reader ''derives'' ms-per-roll from observed rolls over elapsed wall time — a wall reading feeding a cadence (liveness), never a verdict (safety). Lawful under the quarantine, worth watching |
| ''the ahi-kā reading'' (`ahi-ka.ts`) | renders standing as a RATIO of a realm's own pace against an ''independent ambient'' it cannot drive, with an `abstain` floor | the escape from the accrual impossibility, and the ruling's quarantine honored exactly: a reading, never an ordering | it delivers what the ruling assigned to φ-accrual by a different mechanism. The ledger line //"LIVENESS = φ-accrual"// now names a shape the house superseded by ruling (2026-09-11) |
| ''the realm registration `expiry`'' (`realm-bag.ts:114-142`, `:348-352`) | a lease in ROLLS; past it the WRITE side lapses and ''the read side never moves'' | the PIN-shaped `expiry` the charge asks about: an `expiry` field that survives by changing its UNIT, not by leaving | nowhere. And it fails OPEN — a reader naming no pace //"cannot judge, so it never narrows"// — the opposite polarity to the pointer's `nowMs >= expiry` fail-closed-on-a-local-clock |
| ''the outbound bridge's echo SET'' (`outbound-bridge.mem:90`, `:101`; `outbound-bridge.ts`) | an inbound apply MUST NOT re-save; the guard rides a COUNT or a SET of applied titles, //"never a flag"// | the same instinct the lease runs on: a ''monotone recorded fact'' beats an ambient mode. TW5's own `changeCount` stamp reads as a per-title high-water mark | a near-miss worth naming: this SET is exactly the roster-of-moments shape `waking-floor:207` STRUCK for epochs. It stays lawful because it lives ''inside one island for one tick'' and answers //did I just apply this//, never //is this newer// |

''The shape all five share.'' Every one of them puts a ''monotone quantity someone else drives'' under the verdict, and every one of them either counts in a logical unit or NAMES the wall reading as a floor. The oracle pointer sits alone among them in gating a verdict on an un-named local clock.

