!! Questions only the operator answers

''Each one sits where #/silence found no sentence. None of them re-opens "No Global Now".''

# ''Q1 — the fence's API shape.'' Warning (1) mandates that the RESOURCE fence. Does that reach the pure function? Three spellings: ''(a)'' `highWaterVersion` becomes REQUIRED and a fence-less call refuses · ''(b)'' it stays optional and `nowMs` goes optional beside it, curing the asymmetry without conscripting callers (the `device-delegation` precedent) · ''(c)'' a third verdict axis, so a fence-less verify answers //signature-and-lineage only// and never //ok//.
# ''Q2 — the pointer's `expiry` unit.'' Does the oracle/bulb pointer keep a wall-ms backstop ''NAMED'' as the floor (the `clockKind: "wall-floor"` shape), or move to ROLLS against `realmPace` (the `realm-bag.ts` shape), or drop the field entirely and let supersession alone carry it? Note the coupling: a Herm or a browser vessel that wires no realm clock would read every pointer as unexpirable under the rolls spelling.
# ''Q3 — the fail polarity when a reader cannot judge.'' `realm-bag.ts` and `readAhiKa` both fail toward STANDING (//it cannot judge, so it never narrows// · `abstain`). The pointer today fails toward DEAD. Does the house's abstain discipline reach the oracle pointer, or does a public read face warrant the stricter polarity?
# ''Q4 — the ledger line.'' `project_clockless_lease_model.md` still reads `LIVENESS = φ-accrual`, which the 2026-09-11 ruling superseded with the ratio-against-an-ambient. Does that memory line get re-written to the ruling, and does the WITNESS = Roughtime line carry a //cited, unbuilt, roster-tension-named// mark beside it?
# ''Q5 — does this carrier cross.'' It sits at `docs/pono`. If its findings settle, does it move to `api/pono` beside <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/waking-floor">>, or does it stay a mining record and let `waking-floor` carry the law forward alone?

